 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the United Veterans Beacon House to file an application\nfor retroactive real property tax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S8022",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8022-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8022\n\nSPONSOR: LAVALLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the United Veterans Beacon House\nto file an application for retroactive real property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the United Veterans Beacon House to file an application for\nexemption from real property taxes for a certain parcel of land located\nin the town of Brookhaven.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes the town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk, to\naccept from the United Veterans Beacon House, a not-for-profit organiza-\ntion, an application for an exemption from real property taxes for the\nparcel owned by such entity at 89 Smith Lane, Yaphank in the town of\nBrookhaven, county of Suffolk.\n\nIf accepted, the application shall be reviewed as if it had been\nreceived on or before the taxable status date established for such roll.\nThe county of Suffolk may, in its sole discretion, provide for the\nrefund of those taxes paid the United Veterans Beacon House and cancel\nthose taxes, fines, penalties, liens or interest remaining unpaid.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnited Veterans Beacon House (UVBH) is a 501-C-3 not-for-profit organ-\nization that provides housing and supportive services to homeless U.S.\nveterans and non-veteran women, children and men. They manage and\nsupport thirty housing locations, providing safe, clean structured\nliving environments to more than 253 individuals on any given night. Out\nof the 253 beds, 165 are devoted solely to veterans.  The United Veter-\nans Beacon House has successfully helped veterans and families move from\ntransitional/shelter housing to independent permanent housing.\n\nUVBH provides its residents with a host of services that create a foun-\ndation for them to become independent successful members of society.\nSome of the services provided include coordinated all mental and\nemotional counseling visits, coordination of and transportation to\nmedical visits, money management classes and life skill classes. Addi-\ntionally, UVBH organizes and runs a food pantry, thrift shop and medical\nlocker for their community.\n\nIn 2015, the Suffolk County Real Estate Department donated 89 Smith Land\nin the hamlet of Yaphank town of Brookhaven, to the United Veterans\nBeacon House. As of December 2015, UVBH completed the tax-exempt appli-\ncation in the town of Brookhaven for 89 Smith Lane.  This legislation is\nnecessary to authorize the town of Brookhaven to accept an application\nfrom UVBH for exempt status from real property taxes for the parcel\nowned by such entity at 89 Smith Lane, Yaphank in the town of Brookha-\nven, county of Suffolk, for the 2015-16 and 201617 assessment rolls and\nreimburse UVBH for taxes paid within those years.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
